## Known limitations

- **Ethernet link can take minutes.** RTL8211F PHY may spend long time on Gigabit
  auto-negotiation before downshifting to 100Mbps. Measured at 26 s, 128 s and 190 s across
  boots on one unit; on that unit, link partner advertised 10/100 only. To skip Gigabit
  negotiation at cost of capping port: `ethtool -s eth0 speed 100 duplex full autoneg off`.
- **WiFi does not use NetworkManager.** `wlan0` runs under standalone `wpa_supplicant`.
  Use `h96-wifi-connect` or tray icon, not `nmcli`.
- **One HDMI output** (HDMI0). Multichannel HDMI audio not verified.
- **In-browser video decode stays on CPU.** Ubuntu's Chromium lacks V4L2 decoder this
  hardware needs; `ff2mpv` button covers it.
- **CPU voltage cannot be set from userspace.** Regulator voltage is read-only by design;
  opt-in `h96-undervolt` edits device tree per chip and reverts unless confirmed.
- **Big cores top out at 2208 MHz**, where vendor OPP table ends.
- **Kernel arrives with image releases**, not through `apt upgrade`.
- **Anti-cheat titles do not run** under x86-on-arm64 emulation; Steam snap does not work
  on this GPU stack.
- **Power off** enters firmware standby and restarts about 45 s later (hardware watchdog);
  unplug power after shutdown.
- **Plasma (Wayland) session is experimental:** 4K60 video drops frames at 3840x2160
  output, no RGB range control, no VRR.

